# --- IDE / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- Data (keep the folders, ignore the contents) -----------------------------
# Generated books and intermediate tables are reproducible from a seed, so they
# are not version-controlled. data/sample/ IS committed: a fresh clone must be
# able to run something.
#
# NOTE the shape of these rules. An earlier project in this portfolio wrote
# `data/*` here, which silently swallowed its own committed sample and made a
# fresh clone crash. Ignore the two generated directories by name, nothing more.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# --- DuckDB ---
# Ignore the WORKING warehouse by path, not every .duckdb file by extension.
# A blanket `*.duckdb` rule would also exclude data/sample/sample_book.duckdb,
# which is committed on purpose so a fresh clone can run immediately. That is
# precisely the mistake a sister project made with `data/*`, and it was found
# only when a clean clone crashed.
data/processed/*.duckdb
data/processed/*.duckdb.wal
*.duckdb.wal

# --- SAS ---
*.sas7bdat
*.log
*.lst
